From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO accent color picker

Add Settings > Appearance > Accent color, under Theme, with the
mascot: 11 colors that go with the charcoal mascot (Periwinkle, the
default, Lavender, Grape, Rose, Coral, Amber, Lime, Mint, Teal, Sky,
Slate) and Custom, a dialog with hue and vividness sliders and a hex
code. The windows of CromIKO restart in the new color right away.

- Periwinkle keeps the brand palette of CromIKO-Theme.patch. Any
  other color becomes the seed of a Material palette, like the theme
  colors of the new tab page customization, and wins over them.
  Incognito windows and custom tabs keep their own colors.
- The CromIKO cards, links, progress bars and icons (shield card and
  weekly report, continue reading, recent downloads, edit home screen,
  Fire button) now use the theme color, so they follow the accent.
- The CromIKO player and manga mode get the accent from Java and use
  it for their controls and the picker box.
- The mascot, the logo and the lock badge keep their periwinkle star.
- On phones that cannot make color palettes (Android 11 and older,
  some with Android 12), the browser stays periwinkle and a note says
  so; the player and manga mode still use the accent.

